# WebAssembly memories grow where they are, on the host's page
# (`/wasm-memory`) in a machine of 1 GiB, whose script says what it found,
# read through the agent's hands: a memory of at most a gigabyte, and one
# without a maximum, each grown 100 MiB at a time to 600 MiB, keep their
# last word at each step, the buffer the page sees as large as the memory,
# and an access past the end throws, as WebAssembly's must. Each growth
# copies nothing: copied, a memory is held twice as it grows (1.1 GB at the
# last step, which this machine does not have, and the page's process
# would be ended for memory).
web-server
memory 1024
requires web
fail-on "PANIC"
wait-serial "desktop ready" 120
mic-silence 1
agent-connected 120
wait-serial "state: Listening" 30
agent-call app_actions '{"app":"browser"}' 60
wait-serial "browser offers" 10
agent-call use_app '{"app":"browser","action":"open","arguments":{"address":"http://{web}/wasm-memory"}}' 30
wait 10
agent-call use_app '{"app":"browser","action":"read_page"}' 60
agent-result "at most a gigabyte, grew to 9601 pages (600 MiB), kept its last word, threw past its end"
agent-result "without a maximum, grew to 9601 pages (600 MiB), kept its last word, threw past its end"
agent-result "WebAssembly memory checks: passed"
reject-serial "page stopped working"
reject-serial "out of memory"
